# Start: the CLOUD FOLDER editor -- an on-screen keyboard holding the
# current folder. START is OK: the script probes the provider (a few
# seconds) and either changes the setting or refuses.
#
# What the folder-result frame shows depends on the endpoint. On WebDAV,
# where /ROCKNIX/Saves is an ordinary path, OK is accepted and the frame is
# the hub again with CHANGE CLOUD FOLDER focused. On MinIO the same value
# is not a legal bucket name and the frame is the refusal dialog naming the
# reason (#78) -- which the `key x` after it dismisses. Both are a pass;
# read the frame to know which endpoint answered.
#
# No re-send on the OK press: it submits a form that talks to the provider,
# and a second submission is a second probe. If START is eaten the walk
# should say so, not press it again.
key ret
wait-for-change 30 0
settle 20
shot folder-result
key x
wait-for-change
settle
shot after-dismiss
